# THE CHATTER PROBE — does ordinary conversation wake the bot?
#
#   dregg-drive --surface telegram --offering tug --as alice --chat -1001234 \
#       --script dregg-drive/scripts/chatter.drive
#
# `route_text`'s own doc says "ordinary chatter is ignored". That is true of the REPLY and
# was never true of the PAINT: a chat holding persisted-but-unbound sessions resumes and
# REPOSTS every one of them on any non-command message. In a group, an unrelated human
# conversation is a stream of non-command messages.

open
send /open dungeon
press 0

# ── chatter with the chat already BOUND: expected silent ────────────────────
send hey what are you all up to
send lol
send anyway

# ── now unbind by restarting, and chatter again ─────────────────────────────
restart
send hey what are you all up to
send lol
send anyway
